{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והיה לאות על ידכה", :translit "vehayah le'ot al yadekha", :gloss "and it shall be for a sign upon your hand"} {:he "ה' תגין על הה\"א", :translit "h' tagin al ha-heh", :gloss "five tagin upon the heh"} {:he "כנגד ה' פרקים", :translit "keneged h' parashot", :gloss "corresponding to five parashot"} {:he "עד הפרק שמניחין בו תפילין", :translit "ad ha-parashah shemanihim bo tefillin", :gloss "until the parashah in which tefillin are placed"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Five tagin are written on the letter heh of the word ידכה, corresponding to the five scriptural parashot from here until the parashah where tefillin are laid."}], :frame {:text "This verse is one of the four scriptural passages inscribed in tefillin. Menachot 34b teaches that tefillin of the head contain four compartments (batim). The four passages are Exodus 13:1–10 (Kadesh), Exodus 13:11–16 (Vehayah ki yevi'akha), Deuteronomy 6:4–9 (Shema), and Deuteronomy 11:13–21 (Vehayah im shamoa). The verse containing this word, והיה לאות על ידכה (Exodus 13:16), falls within the second of these passages. The present verse is located in the second of the four passages. From this verse forward, the remaining parashot — Vehayah ki yevi'akha, Shema (Deuteronomy 6:4–9), and Vehayah im shamoa (Deuteronomy 11:13–21) — together with the current one, bring the count to the full set of passages associated with tefillin. The five tagin correspond to the sequence of five parashiyot from the beginning of the book of Exodus up to and including this parashah, the one in which the commandment of tefillin is recorded.", :sources ["Menachot 34b" "Exodus 13:16"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ולטוטפת בין עיניך", :translit "uletotafot bein einekha", :gloss "and as totafot between your eyes"} {:he "אלו ארבעה בתים", :translit "elu arba'ah batim", :gloss "these are four compartments"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ולטוטפת", :b "אלו ארבעה בתים"}], :frame {:text "Sanhedrin 4b derives that the word totafot denotes two, so that 'totafot between your eyes' refers to four compartments total. Menachot 34b identifies these as the four batim (compartments) of the head-tefillin, each housing one of four scriptural passages. The Ba'al HaTurim notes that the numerical value of ולטוטפת equals that of אלו ארבעה בתים ('these are four compartments'), encoding this count within the verse itself.", :sources ["Sanhedrin 4b" "Menachot 34b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Five tagin are written on the letter heh of the word ידכה, corresponding to the five scriptural parashot from here until the parashah where tefillin are laid.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "ולטוטפת", :a-value 540, :b "אלו ארבעה בתים", :b-value 767, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:15:39.942714635Z", :model "glm-5.2"}